{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"The current Rust diverges on the two hazardous paths: debug Rust inserts a null-dereference panic, while C performs the machine load directly, and Rust initializes `bad`’s pointer to null while the built C reads the uninitialized stack slot. I’m replacing those exports with x86_64 naked wrappers matching the C function frames and load behavior, then adding a fixed-seed `libloading` integration harness that runs hazardous calls in subprocesses and compares complete process output/status."}}
